meta {
  name: Create Product Family
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Product Family"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.name: eq WC Test Product Family
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 on "David's Dev Account". **Major finding**:
  Product Families were confirmed **read-only** in Phase 3
  (config quirk #38 -- "genuinely read-only, no `POST` anywhere in the
  spec"). The 2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json` refresh adds `POST
  /product-families` (and `PATCH`/`DELETE /product-families/{identifier}`)
  for the first time -- this is a **new capability**, not a
  previously-undeclared-but-working one like most of this session's other
  findings. Confirmed live: it genuinely works now.

  ## What it does
  `POST /product-families` with just `{"name": "..."}` -- `201 Created`.
  The new family immediately gets `total_attributes: 4` with no
  attributes specified in the create body -- these are account-level
  default/system attributes auto-assigned to every family (mirrors
  quirk #30's finding that products get default completeness attributes
  even when not requested).

  `ProductFamilyCreateInputDto` also accepts `attributes` /
  `parent_attributes` / `variant_attributes` arrays (attribute IDs or
  `{id, label}` objects) to link attributes at creation time -- not
  exercised in this session's create call; attribute linking was tested
  separately via the dedicated `/attributes` sub-resource (see
  "Create Family Attribute Link.bru").

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  Family names are unique per account, enforced with **`409`**
  (`AlreadyExists` family, same side of the split as products/attributes/
  channels per quirk #25a/#33/#45a -- NOT categories'/lists' `422` side):
  `{"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists","description":"A Product family with
  same name already exists"}]}`.

  ## Not kept as a fixture
  The family created in this example was renamed and deleted in the same
  session (see "Update and Delete Product Family.bru") -- no new
  Product Families fixture was kept, since the real pre-existing
  "Accessories"/"Apparel"/"Office Supplies" families already cover every
  read-only scenario this collection needs.
}

example {
  name: 201 - Success
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 on "David's Dev Account" -- this family was renamed and deleted later in the same session, not kept as a fixture.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Product Family"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e",
            "name": "WC Test Product Family",
            "total_products": 0,
            "total_attributes": 4,
            "total_models": 1,
            "created": "2026-09-15T16:28:02.086000+00:00",
            "modified": "2026-09-15T16:28:02.090000+00:00"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 201 - Full Parameters
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-22. Exercises every field on ProductFamilyCreateInputDto (name + attributes) in one call. Deleted immediately after capture, not kept as a fixture. See two new findings in the docs block above: (1) attribute references across attributes/parent_attributes/variant_attributes must be ALL plain-ID strings or ALL {id,label} objects -- mixing forms across the three fields 422s; (2) parent_attributes/variant_attributes are blocked by the same "Automatic inheritance is not available for this account" 403 that blocks the PATCH level-change endpoint (see "Update Family Attribute Level.bru") -- only attributes (which always link at no_level) can be populated on this account. All three attribute refs used here (one custom text attribute, two real system attributes) resolved to real attribute_id/level=no_level links, confirmed via a follow-up GET on the attributes collection subpath.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Full Params Family",
        "attributes": [
          {"id": "6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1", "label": "wc_test_text"},
          {"id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19d1", "label": "adult"},
          {"id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19cd", "label": "age_group"}
        ]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6ab2fe5c125f1d0ceeeed6b8",
            "name": "WC Test Full Params Family",
            "total_products": 0,
            "total_attributes": 7,
            "total_models": 1,
            "created": "2026-09-22T22:17:00.683000+00:00",
            "modified": "2026-09-22T22:17:00.797000+00:00"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 422 - Mixed Attribute Reference Forms
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-22. attributes as plain ID strings mixed with parent_attributes/variant_attributes as {id,label} objects -- rejected. New finding, not previously documented in this collection.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Full Params Family",
        "attributes": ["6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1"],
        "parent_attributes": [{"id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19d1", "label": "adult"}],
        "variant_attributes": [{"label": "age_group"}]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "Value error, attributes: attribute references must be either all IDs or all {id, label} objects, not mixed across attributes, parent_attributes, variant_attributes"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 403 - parent_attributes Blocked by Inheritance Gate
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-22, using consistent {id,label} object form across all three arrays (avoiding the mixed-form 422 above). New finding -- the "Automatic inheritance is not available for this account" gate (previously only confirmed on the PATCH level-change endpoint, see status-gating rule #4 in config/api-testing.config.md) also blocks create-time parent_attributes/variant_attributes, not just the level-change PATCH.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Full Params Family",
        "attributes": [{"id": "6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1", "label": "wc_test_text"}],
        "parent_attributes": [{"id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19d1", "label": "adult"}],
        "variant_attributes": [{"id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19cd", "label": "age_group"}]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 403
      text: Forbidden
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "PermissionError",
              "description": "Automatic inheritance is not available for this account"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 409 - Duplicate Name
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, re-creating a family with a name that already existed in this account at the time.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Product Family Renamed"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 409
      text: Conflict
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "AlreadyExists",
              "description": "A Product family with same name already exists"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
